{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_1","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc \"sed -n '1,110p' Makefile; cat host/gambit/ffi/watchdog.sh; uname -s; date -u '+%Y-%m-%d %H:%M:%S GMT'\"","aggregated_output":"# jolt — Clojure on Chez Scheme. Single substrate, no Janet.\n#\n# bin/jolt runs jolt directly off the checked-in seed (host/chez/seed/).\n# `make build` builds the standalone binary, `make test` is the full gate, and\n# `make remint` rebuilds the seed after a source change.\n\nR := https://github.com/makeplus/makes\nM ?= .cache/makes\n# PINNED. Unpinned, this clone is whatever makeplus/makes HEAD is on the day of\n# the build — including a release build, whose toolchain would then be decided by\n# a repository this one records no version of. Bump deliberately.\nV := d14cb578c2f04e6f9d00e01c7c4e416a9baf94e9\n# Nix supplies a locked, source-only tree through M. Ordinary checkouts retain\n# the Git clone so their pinned revision is verified and provisioned on demand.\n$(shell [ -f '$M/init.mk' ] || git clone -q $R '$M')\n# Fetch only when the pin is absent, so a normal build stays offline. A\n# source-only Nix input has no .git directory, so there is nothing to fetch.\n$(shell [ ! -d '$M/.git' ] || { git -C '$M' cat-file -e '$V^{commit}' 2>/dev/null || git -C '$M' fetch -q origin; git -C '$M' rev-parse -q --verify HEAD 2>/dev/null | grep -qx '$V' || git -C '$M' checkout -q '$V'; })\n\ninclude $M/init.mk\n\n# The Chez jolt builds with always carries jolt's kernel patches\n# (host/chez/chez-patches). An explicit CHEZ= or CHEZSCHEME= is authoritative:\n# CI, the release jobs and the nix shell build a patched Chez and pass it in.\n# Otherwise the pinned Chez is built and patched below; a Chez on PATH is never\n# used, since nothing says it carries the patches.\nJOLT-CHEZ := $(or $(CHEZ),$(CHEZSCHEME))\n# bionic (Android's libc) is not readable off a machine tag — Android builds as\n# tarm64le, the same tag as glibc arm64 Linux — so ask the compiler, as\n# build.ss's bld-bionic? does. makes' xPack GCC is a glibc binary, so bionic\n# builds Chez with the host cc below.\nJOLT-BIONIC := $(if $(findstring android,$(shell cc -dumpmachine 2>/dev/null)),1,)\n\nifneq (,$(JOLT-CHEZ))\nSHELL-DEPS += $(JOLT-CHEZ)\nelse ifneq (windows,$(OS-NAME))\n$(eval $(call include-local))\n# The pinned release, patched with host/chez/chez-patches the way every CI and\n# release Chez is, so a from-source build runs the same kernel the releases\n# do. makes' chezscheme.mk can't patch (its one recipe extracts, configures\n# and installs), so host/chez/provision-chez.sh builds it instead; that\n# script says why it stages by hand. The prefix is makes' own layout, so\n# bin/jolt's .cache/local glob finds it, and it is keyed on the patches' hash:\n# the stamp names the patch set, so a prefix built before a patch changed (or\n# before patches were applied here at all) is rebuilt.\n#\n# The compiler: on Linux, makes' xPack GCC; on macOS the host compiler, Apple's\n# clang, as release.yml builds it (xPack GCC 14.2.0-1's fixed <stdio.h> doesn't\n# compile against current macOS SDKs, #1601); on bionic the host cc, since\n# xPack GCC is a glibc binary the Android loader cannot exec.\nifeq (1,$(JOLT-BIONIC))\nCHEZSCHEME-CC := cc\nelse ifeq (macos,$(OS-NAME))\nGCC-LOADED := true\nGCC := $(shell command -v cc)\nCHEZSCHEME-CC := $(GCC)\nelse\ninclude $M/gcc.mk\nCHEZSCHEME-CC := $(GCC)\nCHEZSCHEME-CC-DEP := $(GCC)\nendif\nCHEZSCHEME-VERSION ?= $(or $(shell sed -n 's/^CHEZSCHEME-VERSION ?= *//p' $M/chezscheme.mk | head -n1),10.4.1)\nCHEZSCHEME-LOCAL := $(LOCAL-ROOT)/chezscheme-$(CHEZSCHEME-VERSION)\nCHEZSCHEME := $(CHEZSCHEME-LOCAL)/bin/scheme\nPETITE-CHEZSCHEME := $(CHEZSCHEME-LOCAL)/bin/petite\nCHEZSCHEME-STAMP := $(CHEZSCHEME-LOCAL)/jolt-patches-$(shell sh host/chez/provision-chez.sh --hash)\n$(CHEZSCHEME-STAMP): $(CHEZSCHEME-CC-DEP)\n\t$Q sh host/chez/provision-chez.sh '$(CHEZSCHEME-LOCAL)' '$(CHEZSCHEME-VERSION)' '$(CHEZSCHEME-CC)'\n$(CHEZSCHEME): $(CHEZSCHEME-STAMP)\n\t@:\nSHELL-DEPS += $(CHEZSCHEME)\nJOLT-CHEZ := $(CHEZSCHEME)\nelse\n# Windows: Chez's `make install` doesn't run under MSYS2, so the Windows CI\n# jobs build and lay out a patched Chez themselves and pass it in. Only the\n# targets that need a Chez fail without one.\nJOLT-CHEZ := chez-not-provisioned-on-windows\n.PHONY: $(JOLT-CHEZ)\n$(JOLT-CHEZ):\n\t@echo \"On Windows, build Chez from source with ci/apply-chez-patches.sh and pass it as CHEZ= (see the Windows jobs in .github/workflows/tests.yml)\" >&2\n\t@exit 1\nendif\n\ninclude $M/clean.mk\ninclude $M/shell.mk\n\nMAKES-CLEAN := \\\n  build/ \\\n  target/ \\\n\nMAKES-REALCLEAN := \\\n  .jolt/ \\\n  test/chez/*/.jolt/ \\\n  test/chez/*/*/.jolt/ \\\n\nPREFIX ?= $(if $(IS-ROOT),/usr/local,$(HOME)/.local)\nCHEZ ?= $(JOLT-CHEZ)\n\n# Hand the selected Chez down to bin/jolt, so the targets that shell out to it\n# run the same interpreter as the ones that call $(CHEZ) directly. When make\n# provisions its own Chez, bin/jolt would otherwise have to find it again.\nexport JOLT_CHEZ := $(CHEZ)\n\nifneq (,$(CHEZSCHEME-LOCAL))\n# The provisioned GCC (on macOS, the host cc) built Chez, so the same driver\n# links the standalone binary: gcc.mk puts the bundle's bin FIRST on the\n# exported PATH, but the bundle ships no `cc`, so a bare cc falls through to\n# the distro driver and pairs it with the bundle's older as/ld (#788: gcc 16\n# .base64 into pre-2.43 gas). build.ss bld-cc reads JOLT_CC. A command-line\n# JOLT_CC=... still wins.\n#!/bin/sh\n# External deadline kills the entire gate process group, including make's children.\nexec python3 - \"$@\" <<'PY'\nimport os, signal, subprocess, sys\nseconds = float(sys.argv[1])\np = subprocess.Popen(sys.argv[2:], start_new_session=True)\ntry:\n    status = p.wait(timeout=seconds)\nexcept subprocess.TimeoutExpired:\n    os.killpg(p.pid, signal.SIGKILL)\n    p.wait()\n    print('WATCHDOG: TIMEOUT after %ss: %s' % (seconds, ' '.join(sys.argv[2:])), file=sys.stderr)\n    sys.exit(124)\nsys.exit(status if status >= 0 else 128 - status)\nPY\nDarwin\n2026-11-19 10:32:20 GMT\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_2","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc \"/Library/Developer/CommandLineTools/usr/bin/git status --short --branch; /Library/Developer/CommandLineTools/usr/bin/git log -4 --oneline; sed -n '2060,2195p' Makefile; rg -n -- '-dynamiclib|-shared|-fPIC|\"'^.*(UNAME|uname|IS-DARWIN|IS-LINUX|HOST_OS)'\"' Makefile host/gambit/ffi .cache/makes/os.mk .cache/makes/platform.mk 2>/dev/null; tail -30 p1b-stage1/P1b-linux-provenance.findings.md; rg --files --hidden -g AGENTS.md -g '\"'!.git/**'\"' .\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_2","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc \"/Library/Developer/CommandLineTools/usr/bin/git status --short --branch; /Library/Developer/CommandLineTools/usr/bin/git log -4 --oneline; sed -n '2060,2195p' Makefile; rg -n -- '-dynamiclib|-shared|-fPIC|\"'^.*(UNAME|uname|IS-DARWIN|IS-LINUX|HOST_OS)'\"' Makefile host/gambit/ffi .cache/makes/os.mk .cache/makes/platform.mk 2>/dev/null; tail -30 p1b-stage1/P1b-linux-provenance.findings.md; rg --files --hidden -g AGENTS.md -g '\"'!.git/**'\"' .\"","aggregated_output":"## gambit-ffi-p1b\nbe0710cd p1b-linux: qualify toolchain provenance pins by host platform\n1e5e6331 p1b-stage1-r2: record passing matrix and bridge-link evidence\ne91f26de p1b-stage1-r2: fix byte fallback and apply Argon review items\n8f9047aa Record P1b stage-1 qualification evidence and remaining refusals\n\t  esac; \\\n\telse \\\n\t  $(GAMBIT-SKIP); \\\n\tfi\n\n# ---- P1b-stage1: the gambitffi* gates ----------------------------------------\n#\n# The bounded FFI tier qualified per the standing codex C4 PARTIAL-GO ruling:\n# memory ops, loading, ordinary calls and invocation-local errno capture,\n# behind the ahead-of-time native bridge (host/gambit/ffi/joltffi-bridge.scm,\n# compiled by gsc into build/gambit-ffi/joltffi-bridge.o1). Blocking,\n# callables, runtime signatures and object pinning keep their message-carrying\n# refusals; the gates assert both the witnesses AND the retained refusals.\n#\n# Deterministic bootstrap: every artifact builds from the pinned inputs in\n# host/gambit/ffi/DIGESTS.txt — verified before compiling, output digests\n# recorded after. No ambient .o1/.dylib is ever trusted. The aggregate target\n# is fail-closed: it passes only when all three gate scripts pass, and a gate\n# runs under the P1a-r2 external watchdog (host/gambit/ffi/watchdog.sh, the\n# same pattern the p1a witnesses use) so a frozen VM is a recorded failure,\n# never a hang.\n\nGAMBIT-FFI-DIR := host/gambit/ffi\nGAMBIT-FFI-BUILD := build/gambit-ffi\n\n# the pinned inputs must match the recorded digests BEFORE anything compiles\ngambitffi-verify-digests:\n\t@sh $(GAMBIT-FFI-DIR)/verify-digests.sh \"$(GAMBIT_PREFIX)\"\n\n$(GAMBIT-FFI-BUILD)/joltffi-bridge.o1: gambitffi-force $(GAMBIT-FFI-DIR)/joltffi-bridge.scm \\\n\t\t$(GAMBIT-FFI-DIR)/DIGESTS.txt $(GAMBIT-FFI-DIR)/generated-shims.scm\n\t@$(MAKE) --no-print-directory gambitffi-verify-digests\n\t@mkdir -p $(GAMBIT-FFI-BUILD)\n\t@rm -f $(GAMBIT-FFI-BUILD)/joltffi-bridge.o1 $(GAMBIT-FFI-BUILD)/joltffi-bridge.o[0-9]* \\\n\t       $(GAMBIT-FFI-BUILD)/joltffi-bridge.c $(GAMBIT-FFI-BUILD)/joltffi-bridge.o \\\n\t       $(GAMBIT-FFI-BUILD)/joltffi-bridge.scm\n\tcp $(GAMBIT-FFI-DIR)/joltffi-bridge.scm $(GAMBIT-FFI-DIR)/generated-shims.scm $(GAMBIT-FFI-BUILD)/\n\tcd $(GAMBIT-FFI-BUILD) && sh ../../$(GAMBIT-FFI-DIR)/watchdog.sh 120 $(GAMBIT_GSC) -dynamic -keep-temp joltffi-bridge.scm\n\t@shasum -a 256 $(GAMBIT-FFI-BUILD)/joltffi-bridge.o1 \\\n\t  > $(GAMBIT-FFI-BUILD)/joltffi-bridge.o1.sha256\n\t@cc --version > $(GAMBIT-FFI-BUILD)/compiler.txt\n\t@shasum -a 256 $(GAMBIT_GSC) $(GAMBIT_GSI) \"$(GAMBIT_PREFIX)/include/gambit.h\" \\\n\t  \"$(GAMBIT_PREFIX)/lib/libgambit.a\" > $(GAMBIT-FFI-BUILD)/runtime.sha256\n\n$(GAMBIT-FFI-BUILD)/libjoltffi-fixture.dylib: gambitffi-force $(GAMBIT-FFI-DIR)/joltffi-fixture.c \\\n\t\t$(GAMBIT-FFI-DIR)/DIGESTS.txt\n\t@$(MAKE) --no-print-directory gambitffi-verify-digests\n\t@mkdir -p $(GAMBIT-FFI-BUILD)\n\tsh $(GAMBIT-FFI-DIR)/watchdog.sh 60 cc -O1 -dynamiclib -o $(GAMBIT-FFI-BUILD)/libjoltffi-fixture.dylib \\\n\t  $(GAMBIT-FFI-DIR)/joltffi-fixture.c\n\t@shasum -a 256 $(GAMBIT-FFI-BUILD)/libjoltffi-fixture.dylib \\\n\t  > $(GAMBIT-FFI-BUILD)/libjoltffi-fixture.dylib.sha256\n\n$(GAMBIT-FFI-BUILD)/libjoltffi-fixture2.dylib: gambitffi-force $(GAMBIT-FFI-DIR)/joltffi-fixture2.c \\\n\t\t$(GAMBIT-FFI-DIR)/DIGESTS.txt\n\t@$(MAKE) --no-print-directory gambitffi-verify-digests\n\t@mkdir -p $(GAMBIT-FFI-BUILD)\n\tsh $(GAMBIT-FFI-DIR)/watchdog.sh 60 cc -O1 -dynamiclib -o $(GAMBIT-FFI-BUILD)/libjoltffi-fixture2.dylib \\\n\t  $(GAMBIT-FFI-DIR)/joltffi-fixture2.c\n\t@shasum -a 256 $(GAMBIT-FFI-BUILD)/libjoltffi-fixture2.dylib \\\n\t  > $(GAMBIT-FFI-BUILD)/libjoltffi-fixture2.dylib.sha256\n\n# the present-but-unloadable candidate: a one-symbol dylib linked against a\n# dependency dylib this recipe then REMOVES, so dlopen fails with the loader's\n# own preserved reason (a missing dependency, not a missing file)\n$(GAMBIT-FFI-BUILD)/libjoltffi-unloadable.dylib: gambitffi-force $(GAMBIT-FFI-DIR)/DIGESTS.txt \\\n\t\t$(GAMBIT-FFI-DIR)/joltffi-dep.c $(GAMBIT-FFI-DIR)/joltffi-unloadable.c\n\t@$(MAKE) --no-print-directory gambitffi-verify-digests\n\t@mkdir -p $(GAMBIT-FFI-BUILD)\n\tsh $(GAMBIT-FFI-DIR)/watchdog.sh 60 cc -O1 -dynamiclib -o $(GAMBIT-FFI-BUILD)/libjoltffi-dep.dylib $(GAMBIT-FFI-DIR)/joltffi-dep.c\n\tsh $(GAMBIT-FFI-DIR)/watchdog.sh 60 cc -O1 -dynamiclib -o $(GAMBIT-FFI-BUILD)/libjoltffi-unloadable.dylib \\\n\t  $(GAMBIT-FFI-DIR)/joltffi-unloadable.c $(GAMBIT-FFI-BUILD)/libjoltffi-dep.dylib\n\trm $(GAMBIT-FFI-BUILD)/libjoltffi-dep.dylib\n\t@shasum -a 256 $(GAMBIT-FFI-BUILD)/libjoltffi-unloadable.dylib \\\n\t  > $(GAMBIT-FFI-BUILD)/libjoltffi-unloadable.dylib.sha256\n\n# bridge + fixtures, always current: the entry every gambitffi gate depends on\n.PHONY: gambitffi-force gambitffi-verify-digests\ngambitffi-force:\n\ngambitffi-bridge: gambitffi-verify-digests $(GAMBIT-FFI-BUILD)/joltffi-bridge.o1 \\\n                  $(GAMBIT-FFI-BUILD)/libjoltffi-fixture.dylib \\\n                  $(GAMBIT-FFI-BUILD)/libjoltffi-fixture2.dylib \\\n                  $(GAMBIT-FFI-BUILD)/libjoltffi-unloadable.dylib\n\ngambitffi-abi: gambitffi-bridge\n\t@if [ -x \"$(GAMBIT_GSI)\" ]; then \\\n\t\tsh $(GAMBIT-FFI-DIR)/watchdog.sh 120 \"$(GAMBIT_GSI)\" $(GAMBIT-FFI-DIR)/gambitffi-abi.ss && \\\n\t\tsh $(GAMBIT-FFI-DIR)/watchdog.sh 180 \"$(GAMBIT_GSI)\" $(GAMBIT-FFI-DIR)/gambitffi-public.ss; \\\n\telse \\\n\t\techo \"$@: required Gambit runtime is absent\" >&2; exit 1; \\\n\tfi\n\n\n$(GAMBIT-FFI-BUILD)/capture-test/joltffi-bridge.o1: $(GAMBIT-FFI-BUILD)/joltffi-bridge.o1\n\t@mkdir -p $(GAMBIT-FFI-BUILD)/capture-test\n\t@rm -f $(GAMBIT-FFI-BUILD)/capture-test/joltffi-bridge.o[0-9]*\n\tcp $(GAMBIT-FFI-DIR)/joltffi-bridge.scm $(GAMBIT-FFI-DIR)/generated-shims.scm $(GAMBIT-FFI-BUILD)/capture-test/\n\tcd $(GAMBIT-FFI-BUILD)/capture-test && sh ../../../$(GAMBIT-FFI-DIR)/watchdog.sh 120 $(GAMBIT_GSC) -dynamic -keep-temp -cc-options -DJOLTFFI_CAPTURE_TEST joltffi-bridge.scm\n\t@shasum -a 256 $(GAMBIT-FFI-BUILD)/capture-test/joltffi-bridge.o1 > $(GAMBIT-FFI-BUILD)/capture-test/joltffi-bridge.o1.sha256\n\ngambitffi-errno-check: gambitffi-bridge $(GAMBIT-FFI-BUILD)/capture-test/joltffi-bridge.o1\n\t@if [ -x \"$(GAMBIT_GSI)\" ]; then \\\n\t\tsh $(GAMBIT-FFI-DIR)/watchdog.sh 120 \"$(GAMBIT_GSI)\" $(GAMBIT-FFI-DIR)/gambitffi-errno.ss; \\\n\telse \\\n\t\techo \"$@: required Gambit runtime is absent\" >&2; exit 1; \\\n\tfi\n\ngambitffi-load-failure-smoke: gambitffi-bridge\n\t@if [ -x \"$(GAMBIT_GSI)\" ]; then \\\n\t\tsh $(GAMBIT-FFI-DIR)/watchdog.sh 90 \"$(GAMBIT_GSI)\" $(GAMBIT-FFI-DIR)/gambitffi-load-failure.ss; \\\n\telse \\\n\t\techo \"$@: required Gambit runtime is absent\" >&2; exit 1; \\\n\tfi\n\n# the aggregate: all three, fail-closed (each script exits nonzero on failure)\ngambitffi: gambitffi-abi gambitffi-errno-check gambitffi-load-failure-smoke\n\t@echo \"gambitffi: PASS — all stage-1 qualified-tier gates green\"\n\n# The browser bundle: the whole stack (kernel + seed + compiler + a queue-polling\n# REPL loop) compiled to one JavaScript file by the Gambit backend. ~30s, ~32MB\n# raw / ~4MB gzipped, which is what a web server ships. Point GAMBIT_WEB_OUT at\n# a site checkout to refresh the live demo:\n#   make gambitweb GAMBIT_WEB_OUT=../jolt-lang.github.io/resources/static/js/jolt-web.js\n# NEVER bare gsc — that is Ghostscript on a brew machine.\n# PROFILE selects how much of the language the bundle carries (host/gambit/\n# profiles.ss lists them: full, repl, kernel). gen-boot.ss writes the boot for it\n# on Chez — Gambit resolves ##include at expansion time, so this cannot be a\n# runtime switch — and binds every name an excluded group owned to a raise that\n# names the group.\nPROFILE ?= full\nGAMBIT_WEB_OUT ?= target/gambit/jolt-web.js\ngambitweb:\n\t@if [ -x \"$(GAMBIT_GSC)\" ]; then \\\n\t\t$(CHEZ) --script host/gambit/gen-boot.ss $(PROFILE); \\\n\t\tmkdir -p \"$$(dirname \"$(GAMBIT_WEB_OUT)\")\"; \\\nMakefile:595:# default), and --dynamic keeps the runtime load-shared-object path.\nMakefile:612:# `uname -r`). shelloutcheck is the static half of the same rule.\nMakefile:1684:\t@$(CHEZ) --script test/chez/vfasl-shared-strings-test.ss\nMakefile:2108:\tsh $(GAMBIT-FFI-DIR)/watchdog.sh 60 cc -O1 -dynamiclib -o $(GAMBIT-FFI-BUILD)/libjoltffi-fixture.dylib \\\nMakefile:2117:\tsh $(GAMBIT-FFI-DIR)/watchdog.sh 60 cc -O1 -dynamiclib -o $(GAMBIT-FFI-BUILD)/libjoltffi-fixture2.dylib \\\nMakefile:2129:\tsh $(GAMBIT-FFI-DIR)/watchdog.sh 60 cc -O1 -dynamiclib -o $(GAMBIT-FFI-BUILD)/libjoltffi-dep.dylib $(GAMBIT-FFI-DIR)/joltffi-dep.c\nMakefile:2130:\tsh $(GAMBIT-FFI-DIR)/watchdog.sh 60 cc -O1 -dynamiclib -o $(GAMBIT-FFI-BUILD)/libjoltffi-unloadable.dylib \\\nhost/gambit/ffi/test-toolchain.py:40:                patch.object(toolchain.os, \"uname\", return_value=host or self.linux), \\\nhost/gambit/ffi/test-toolchain.py:119:        self.assertIn(\"invalid uname platform key\", err)\nhost/gambit/ffi/toolchain.py:20:    host = os.uname()\nhost/gambit/ffi/toolchain.py:25:        raise ValueError(\"invalid uname platform key: \" + repr(key))\nhost/gambit/ffi/ffi-harness.ss:64:  (sa-load-shared-object ffi-fixture-path))\nhost/gambit/ffi/gambitffi-abi.ss:18:             (sa-load-shared-object ffi-fixture-path)\nhost/gambit/ffi/README.md:49:from `uname` via Python's `os.uname()`: lowercase OS and architecture, with\nhost/gambit/ffi/README.md:91:existing fixture recipes use Darwin `-dynamiclib` flags; this provenance-only\nhost/gambit/ffi/gambitffi-load-failure.ss:16:                 (sa-load-shared-object \"/nonexistent/libjoltffi-nope.dylib\")\nhost/gambit/ffi/gambitffi-load-failure.ss:19:                    (sa-load-shared-object \"build/gambit-ffi/libjoltffi-unloadable.dylib\")\nhost/gambit/ffi/gambitffi-load-failure.ss:55:(sa-load-shared-object ffi-fixture2-path)\nhost/gambit/ffi/joltffi-bridge.scm:69:{ return ___CAST(unsigned long, dlopen (path, JOLTFFI_RTLD_NOW)); }   /* sa-load-shared-object of #f */\n- Ten standard-library unit/integration checks passed (120s watchdog). Linux\n  host metadata and install files in these checks are synthetic fixtures,\n  not Linux execution or qualification. They exercise acceptance of an\n  explicitly recorded Linux manifest; rejection of missing Linux pins despite\n  existing Darwin pins; wrong header; changed binary; missing/duplicate/extra\n  rows; unknown/invalid platform; deterministic content-only recording;\n  no replacement after a missing input; and unindexed manifest rejection.\n- Original Darwin pin comparison passed (15s watchdog): all seven old digests\n  preserved, not replaced with different pins.\n- `make gambitffi` passed (300s watchdog, JOLT_REQUIRE_GAMBIT=1), selecting the\n  Darwin manifest and checking every source/manifest digest before builds.\n\n```text\ngambitffi: platform=darwin-arm64 manifest=host/gambit/ffi/TOOLCHAIN.darwin-arm64.sha256\ngambitffi: toolchain verified (7 inputs)\ngambitffi-abi: 78 check(s), 0 failure(s)\ngambitffi-public: 44 check(s), 0 failure(s)\ngambitffi-errno-check: 9 check(s), 0 failure(s)\ngambitffi-load-failure-smoke: 14 check(s), 0 failure(s)\ngambitffi: PASS — all stage-1 qualified-tier gates green\n```\n\nNo Linux runtime, ABI or consumer qualification is claimed. The orchestrator\nrecords actual shiva pins and reruns its Linux matrix. A likely next Linux\nbuild issue remains visible in the existing fixture rec